    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Step 1: Recognize that the given expression can be factored into differences of squares.\nStep 2: Group the terms into pairs and apply the factoring formula (a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)).\nStep 3: Simplify the factored expression.\nStep 4: Calculate the final value.\n\nSolution with the steps introduced:\nThe expression is given as \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\). We can group the terms like this: \\((19^2 - 17^2) + (15^2 - 13^2) + (11^2 - 9^2) + (7^2 - 5^2) + (3^2 - 1^2)\\).\n\nStep 2:\nNow, let's factor the differences of squares using the formula \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a^2 - b^2) = (a + b)(a - b)\\).\n\nFor \\(19^2 - 17^2\\):\n\\(19^2 - 17^2 = (19 + 17)(19 - 17) = 36 \\cdot 2 = 72\\)\n\nFor \\(15^2 - 13^2\\):\n\\(15^2 - 13^2 = (15 + 13)(15 - 13) = 28 \\cdot 2 = 56\\)\n\nFor \\(11^2 - 9^2\\):\n\\(11^2 - 9^2 = (11 + 9)(11 - 9) = 20 \\cdot 2 = 40\\)\n\nFor \\(7^2 - 5^2\\):\n\\(7^2 - 5^2 = (7 + 5)(7 - 5) = 12 \\cdot 2 = 24\\)\n\nFor \\(5^2 - 1^2\\):\n\\(5^2 - 1^2 = (5 + 1)(5 - 1) = 6 \\cdot 4 = 24\\)\n\nNow, we will simplify:\n\\(72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 24\\)\n\nStep 3:\nAdd the terms together:\n\\(72 + 56 = 128\\)\n\\(40 + 24 = 64\\)\n\\(128 + 64 = 192\\)\n\nStep 4:\nWe have the final answer.\nThe value of \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{192}\\).",
